WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:05.200 --> 00:00:11.920
August 13, 2021, marks the 60th anniversary of&nbsp;
the Berlin Wall. Why was it built, and what does&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:11.920 --> 00:00:17.360
it say about our world today? Following World War&nbsp;
II, the forces that defeated the Nazis divvied up&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:17.360 --> 00:00:24.960
Germany, and in 1949 East Germany was established.&nbsp;
Conditions were oppressive, and by July 1961,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:24.960 --> 00:00:30.320
millions of East Germans had left for West&nbsp;
Germany, with around 1,000 more leaving every day.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:30.320 --> 00:00:33.760
While the border between East and&nbsp;
West Germany was already well guarded,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:33.760 --> 00:00:39.120
passage from East Berlin to West Berlin remained&nbsp;
an easy loophole. To prevent further emigration,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:39.120 --> 00:00:45.040
East Germany built a wall surrounding West&nbsp;
Berlin. For the next 28 years, the wall ensured&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:45.040 --> 00:00:51.200
that few East Germans escaped. Today, different&nbsp;
countries are erecting walls of a digital kind,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:51.200 --> 00:00:56.560
but such walls are not impassable, and they are&nbsp;
not permanent. Regimes may have the power to shut&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:56.560 --> 00:01:03.120
their populations in, but East Germany's efforts&nbsp;
suggest they'll ultimately fail. That's a powerful&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:03.120 --> 00:01:11.360
message to today's authoritarians. Is the world&nbsp;
freer today than it was in 1961? Let us know in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:11.360 --> 00:01:16.960
our poll, and also let us know which other topics&nbsp;
you'd like our scholars to explain in 60 seconds,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:17.680 --> 00:01:22.000
and be sure to like and subscribe for&nbsp;
more research and videos from AEI.

